कर-ग्रहण (णं) 1.
n. Taking the hand;
marriage; taking tax.

करण्ड (ण्डः) 1.
m. A basket or covered
box of bamboo wicker work;
[]
bee hive; honey comb; a sword;
a duck; Valesneria.

करो_त्कर (रः) 1.
m. A bundle of rags;
a very heavy tax.

कर्पूर-मणि (णिः) 1.
m. A white gem;
a medicinal mineral.

कर्म्म-त्याग (गः) 1.
m. Giving up works;
abandoning the world.

कर्म्मन् (र्म्मा-र्म्म) 5.
m. n. Action;
work; objective case.

कर्म्म-योग (गः) 1.
m. Doing duty;
activity, industry.

कर्म्मा_न्त (न्तः) 1.
m. End of works;
object of works; tilled land.

कर्म्मा_न्तर (रं) 1.
n. Opposing duty;
suspense; penance.

कारुष (षः) 1.
m. The offspring of
an outcast of the
Vaisya tribe;
a country;
plu. Its people.
